cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "ai-augmented-agents (work in progress)"
abstract: >-
  Several agents, people and language models, on one project: delegation, coordination and incentives, with the tools of game theory, team theory and multi-agent reinforcement learning. A first review pass of 35 sources is written.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/ai-augmented-agents"
license:
